c072285f2"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-35-15","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":35,"verse":15,"english":"Rāghava has in him, O monkeys, energy, manliness, strength, kindness, gratitude and prowess.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-37-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5035015","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"51b1e1b81a57dbae9e2b8050a6df0af1dfa4ef4bc3d051ac8a676841e428f7a1","compact":"692e4441fdafe7da4bda01757888698ae09886b9d5c1134c36733f7378041033","nasal":"45032e28183b90934f4fe17bee793c75e74e1e7b3edac34512dd65b22639f438"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-35-16","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":35,"verse":16,"english":"He brought about without his brother's aid, the destruction of the fourteen thousand Rākṣasas at Janasthāna. What enemy is not troubled at this?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-37-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5035016","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3e85ed77cd308491e731a88ac2950fb7e52d17736ddbdc024fa6bbc51e406073","compact":"284148acd273a9809e46ed47badda0787fc9e84e940b0772e3fec05b8e284b16","nasal":"284148acd273a9809e46ed47badda0787fc9e84e940b0772e3fec05b8e284b16"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-35-17","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":35,"verse":17,"english":"The disaster-creating Rākşasas can never be compared with that best of men. I am cognizant of his prowess as Sacī is of Indra's.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-37-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5035017","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6e09cab6b481fbec96d745ac6abb5a020f65511b3264149c9bada91976a3d0a0","compact":"410889cfc2220f3f27c566f4486ed57b22829ac6833cbca9e8623